# Gitflow

- `main` is release-only; do normal work from feature branches branched from `develop`.
- Branch `feature/*` and `bugfix/*` from `develop`, then open focused PRs back to `develop`.
- Cut releases by merging `develop` into `main` and tagging the release on `main`.
- Branch `hotfix/*` from `main`; merge hotfixes into both `main` and `develop`.
- Do not commit, push, merge, tag, or create a PR unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Keep branches and PRs narrowly scoped; exclude unrelated cleanup and user changes.
